<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Naumburg Master</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naumburg">Naumburg</a> Master is the name given to an anonymous sculptor and architect, trained in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, who worked at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a>, Naumburg and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meissen">Meissen</a> in the mid-13th century. His statues of the founders in the west choir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naumburg-cathedral">Naumburg Cathedral</a>, made around 1250, are among the masterpieces of Gothic sculpture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/naumburg-master.jpg" alt="Naumburg Master" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Josep Renalias · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Est%C3%A0tues_fundadors_de_Naumburg.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
